{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY4LcjAhY3Tet2gjne7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading of the board, before any model is written.\n\nQuestion the board answers: who does what on a Roamstay damage claim, where it changes hands, and what status it holds at each step?\nOutcome: the Roamstay product and support team can check each hand-off and status against the claims policy.\nDials: Faithful detail, Mixed audience, Laptop distance.\n\nSource and class: the claims policy, current behavior. The under-25-euro waiver is not live and stays off the board. The policy says nothing about day 7 passing with no reply, so that stays off too.\n\nAssumed, with what would settle each:\n- Reader and outcome: the Roamstay product and support team, from your \"use the recommended answers\". The board owner naming the real reader would settle it\n- Who charges the card: the policy gives no actor, so the charge steps sit in the Roamstay support lane. The policy owner naming who triggers the charge would settle it\n\nOutline, in drawing order:\n1. Hotel lane: Report the damage (start). Photos and a repair quote from a listed supplier. Moves the claim to Reported\n2. Support lane: Send claim to guest. The guest sees the photos, the quote and the amount in the app. Moves the claim to With the guest\n3. Guest lane: Accept or dispute? (the highlighted decision, 7 days to answer)\n4. Accept: Support lane, Charge the card on file\n5. Dispute: Support lane, Review photos and reply. Reads the photos and the guest's reply, and asks the hotel for more photos if they do not show the damage. Moves the claim to Under review\n6. Decision: Uphold or drop? Support decides within 5 working days\n7. Uphold: Charge the card on file, within 2 working days\n8. Drop, and both charge steps, end at Claim closed. That end moves the claim to Closed\n9. Status lane on top: Reported, With the guest, Under review, Closed, with a dotted line from each step that moves the claim\n\nThat is 12 nodes and 16 connectors in four lanes, inside the Faithful budget.\n\nTwo framings:\n- Lanes plus a status lane, which shows the hand-offs and the status at each step. It costs a wider board. I recommend it\n- A state map of the claim alone, which shows every status exit. It loses who acts at each step\n\nThe more-photos request sits in the review step's detail and not as a loop of its own. The policy does not say what the hotel does next or what status the claim holds meanwhile, and a loop would invent both.\n\nLook:\n- The highlight falls on Accept or dispute?, with the reason \"the guest decides\"\n- The goal is Claim closed\n- The title is \"Roamstay damage claim\"\n- The subtitle is \"From the hotel's damage report to a closed claim, for the Roamstay product and support team\"\n- The source line is \"Source: Roamstay claims policy. Left out: the under-25-euro waiver (not live), day 7 passing with no reply\"\n\nDoes this reading match the policy, or should I correct a row?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5672,"cache_read_input_tokens":84207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5672},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b87d0f72-2de5-4ea9-bb3b-56f4ce82980a","uuid":"ea3646b5-343d-47ac-b54a-4cad42d688bf","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:52:39.770Z","request_id":"req_011CgY4LcP5oeafbUqfGuez9"}
